/T (The OHS Committee is tasked with a range of responsibilities to identify and address potential hazards within the workplace. This includes conducting regular workplace inspections as required by regulations, where the committee can assess the safety of the environment and identify aspects that may contribute to health risks. The committee engages with various stakeholders providing recommendations aimed at improving safety standards and ensuring compliance with established regulations. The committee also receives and addresses complaints from employees regarding health and safety concerns, creating open dialogue and developing a culture of safety within the workplace.They are to maintain meticulous records of complaints and their resolution to ensure accountability and transparency in addressing health and safety matters. )
/E (The OHS Committee is tasked with a range of responsibilities to identify and address potential hazards within the workplace. This includes conducting regular workplace inspections as required by regulations, where the committee can assess the safety of the environment and identify aspects that may contribute to health risks. The committee engages with various stakeholders providing recommendations aimed at improving safety standards and ensuring compliance with established regulations. The committee also receives and addresses complaints from employees regarding health and safety concerns, creating open dialogue and developing a culture of safety within the workplace.They are to maintain meticulous records of complaints and their resolution to ensure accountability and transparency in addressing health and safety matters. )
