/T (Up to 52 weeks of unpaid leave will be given to the employee in relation to the disappearance of a child and up to 104 weeks of unpaid leave in relation to the death of a child. The duration of leave must be limited to that which is reasonably necessary in the circumstances. The employee must be employed with Barrio Legado for at least 30 days, must be the parent of a child under the age of 18 who has disappeared or died and it is probable, considering the circumstances, that the child disappeared or died as a result of a crime under the Federal Criminal Code, and they must not have been charged with the crime necessitating the leave. The employee must provide reasonable verification of the necessity of the leave as soon as possible as well as give two weeks written notice of the intended amount and date leave will begin, unless there is a valid reason why that notice cannot be given.Upon returning to work, the employee will be placed in the same or a similar position with the same duties, benefits, and wages they had before their leave.)
