1411 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 591 0 R
/T (Safety Data Sheets \(SDSs\) are comprehensive documents that detail the hazards associated with a product and offer guidance on safety precautions. Typically authored by the manufacturer or supplier, SDSs are required to be provided by suppliers of hazardous products at the time of sale. Safety Data Sheets \(SDSs\) offer comprehensive hazard information regarding products, exceeding the details provided on labels. They serve as a vital resource for workplaces and employees concerning the products utilized. It is essential to consult this information to identify the associated hazards and adhere to the recommended safe handling and emergency procedures to ensure the protection of workers from these hazards. SDSs tell users what the hazards of the product are, how to use the product safely, what to expect if the recommendations are not followed, how to recognize symptoms of exposure, and what to do if emergencies occur.)
/E (Safety Data Sheets \(SDSs\) are comprehensive documents that detail the hazards associated with a product and offer guidance on safety precautions. Typically authored by the manufacturer or supplier, SDSs are required to be provided by suppliers of hazardous products at the time of sale. Safety Data Sheets \(SDSs\) offer comprehensive hazard information regarding products, exceeding the details provided on labels. They serve as a vital resource for workplaces and employees concerning the products utilized. It is essential to consult this information to identify the associated hazards and adhere to the recommended safe handling and emergency procedures to ensure the protection of workers from these hazards. SDSs tell users what the hazards of the product are, how to use the product safely, what to expect if the recommendations are not followed, how to recognize symptoms of exposure, and what to do if emergencies occur.)
/Pg 70 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
