/T (Chemicals pose a risk to human health through various exposure routes, including inhalation, dermal contact, ingestion, and injection. Their effects can vary significantly, leading to issues ranging from immediate irritation to long-term health conditions such as cancer, organ failure, and hormonal disruption. These substances can interfere with biological processes by functioning as toxins, asphyxiants, or endocrine disruptors.)
/E (Chemicals pose a risk to human health through various exposure routes, including inhalation, dermal contact, ingestion, and injection. Their effects can vary significantly, leading to issues ranging from immediate irritation to long-term health conditions such as cancer, organ failure, and hormonal disruption. These substances can interfere with biological processes by functioning as toxins, asphyxiants, or endocrine disruptors.)
/Pg 72 0 R
/K [8]
