/Title (As part of our commitment to maintaining an efficient and organized workplace, we ask that all staff members be prepared to start their shifts at least 5 minutes before their scheduled start time. This practice ensures that you are in uniform, equipped with all necessary tools, and have your personal belongings stored away prior to clocking in. As part of our commitment to maintaining accurate timekeeping, it is essential that staff members clock out before attending to personal items or preparing to leave for the day. We utilize the Push Operations App for tracking work hours, and it is each employee's responsibility to clock in and out for every shift. If you find yourself in a situation where you've forgotten to clock in or out, please inform your manager or supervisor as soon as possible so that we can make the necessary adjustments. Timely communication is key to ensuring that everyone is accurately compensated for their hours worked. We also encourage staff members to regularly review their hours worked against their timesheets and pay. If you notice any discrepancies or have questions regarding your hours, please do not hesitate to reach out to your manager.)
