/Title (Hazardous materials are substances, solid, liquid, or gas, that present significant risks to health, safety, property, or the environment throughout their production, handling, or transportation processes. Suppliers are required to evaluate their products against the criteria outlined in the Hazardous Products Regulations. Should a product satisfy any criteria for a hazard class, it will be classified as a WHMIS-regulated hazardous product. All hazardous products must be appropriately labeled in accordance with the Hazardous Products Regulations, and a corresponding safety data sheet must be provided to the purchaser at the time of sale.)
