<<
/Title (A workplace incident report is an official document that captures details about injuries, illnesses, near misses, or property damage that occur on the job. This report plays a crucial role in safety, compliance, and risk management. To ensure the information is accurate, reports are to be filled out within 24 hours, documenting the who, what, when, and where of the incident. These reports are essential for maintaining legal and safety regulatory compliance, identifying potential hazards to prevent future incidents, and providing necessary information for insurance claims.)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5119 0 R
/Next 5126 0 R
>>
endobj
5126 0 obj
<<
/Title (When completing the report, please ensure that you include the following essential details: the date and time of the incident, the precise location, the names of any injured parties and witnesses, a factual step-by-step account of what occurred, and any immediate actions taken, such as first aid or reporting. Additionally, please attach any relevant photos, sketches, or documents. If the injured party or any witnesses are not employed by the company, get their contact information in case they need to be contacted. After the incident, it is important  to ensure that anyone injured receives appropriate medical attention, secure the scene to prevent further occurrences, and notify a supervisor or manager.)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5119 0 R
/Prev 5125 0 R
>>
endobj
